\begin{align*}
ax + cz &= 2a, \\
ay + cw &= b, \\
bx + dw &= 2c, \\
by + dw &= d.
\end{align*}
Since the equation must hold for all $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$, we can solve the first and last equations for $x$ and $z$:
\begin{align*}
ax + cz &= 2a \implies x = 2, z = 0, \\
by + dw &= d \implies w = 0.
\end{align*}
Substituting these into the remaining equations, we get:
\begin{align*}
ay + cw &= b \implies ay = b \implies y = 1, \\
bx + dw &= 2c \implies bx = 2c \implies x = 2.
\end{align*}
